// The source of the moves of `npc_ramen_nujan`: Ramen-nujan as a fighter.
// The game loads this file through the content pack (`assets/pack.ron`); edit it here.
// Its grab boxes are stated for its standing height (65.0), not for the 48 of a
// row that states none: a grab is the reach of the body, so it grows with the body.
//
// DESIGN NOTES.
//
// He fights with his MATHEMATICS, and it is written at arm's length from him:
// each blow is a chalk-gold symbol a little way past his hand, so his own body
// is seldom in the blow. He is light: what hits him sends him far. He keeps
// you out (the partition, the scarf), and he is in trouble when you are in.
//
// His normals are terms of a sum (a sigma, an infinity, a factorial). His
// smashes are the factorial (forward and up) and the seal of -1/12 (down); he
// holds one the way a theorem arrives, with his eyes shut. His GRAB is his
// scarf: it reaches far for a grab and a miss is long.
//
// His specials. Neutral: a partition (the noodle goes out with a sigma on its
// end). Side: 1729 (he goes forward; two blows). Up: a divergent series (each
// term is a step up; a save, not a flight). Down: -1/12 (a counter). Down in
// the air: convergence (he comes down on the seal).
//
// FIRST CUT, 2026-10-12. The format is GNU-ton's table's. Each move's live
// window is the part of its sheet row where the symbol is drawn (a row is
// slaved to its move: frame = progress x frames). Each volume is on the side
// of him where the row draws the symbol, and is wider than the picture, as
// the roster's are. Damage, launch and the lengths of the moves are a start
// for play, not a result of it. His own hit effects are not made: each blow
// draws the common slash.
